  "releaseNotes": "- feat: inline collection lambdas are lifted into per-element connectors — `coll |> List.map (fun x -> …)` over a RECORD element now generates the same adaptive structure as a named `[<PureView>]` sub-view (a nested child module with its own `Input`/`Connector`/`compiled`, fed by a `ChangeableModelList`), instead of coarse plain splicing. Works at the top level, nested, AND inside DU case arms (the case binder is registered as an adaptive collection var so it flows through the same path). The analyzer now analyses every body uniformly (`analyzeTypedBody`) and recurses into the lambdas it lifts; a reference-GC emits only the children the final body actually calls (drops speculative cross-case synthesis). Verified end-to-end with real fsc + runtime reactive add/switch.",
  "title": "Adaptify.PureView",
  "verbatimVersion": "0.1.15",
